Callable after find_tools:
- search_shipments — List shipments, optionally narrowed by free text such as a pro number, BOL, customer name, or city, and by status.
- get_worker — Retrieve one worker (driver) by id, including their profile and current state.
- search_worker — List workers (drivers), optionally narrowed by a name or code.
- list_expiring_credentials — List worker (driver) credentials falling due, newest expiry first — medical cards, licences, hazmat endorsements and anything else the organization tracks.
- list_time_off — List worker (driver) time-off requests — who is out, who is asking to be, and who was turned down.
- list_hold_reasons — List the reasons a shipment can be put on hold, and what each one blocks — dispatch, delivery, billing.
- shop_carriers — Price a saved shipment against carriers and rank them by contract cost, margin against the customer's charge, and routing guide rank.
- place_shipment_hold — Put a shipment on hold so it stops moving, billing or delivering until someone clears it.
- release_shipment_hold — Clear a hold so the shipment can move again.
- update_tractor_status — Change the status of one or more tractors, which is what makes a truck available to dispatch or takes it off the board.
- update_trailer_status — Change the status of one or more trailers, which is what makes a trailer available to dispatch or takes it off the board.
- list_insights — List insight detector findings: service slipping for a customer, cash tied up in unbilled work, cost leaking at a location, compliance about to lapse.
- get_insight — Read one insight in full: the finding with its numbers and records, its earlier runs, and the rule behind it.
- unassign_moves — Take the driver and equipment off one or more moves that have not started, leaving each uncovered for someone else.
- update_move_status — Set the status of one or more moves directly: InTransit when a load is rolling, Completed when it has been delivered, Canceled when the move will not run.
- assign_move_to_carrier — Cover a move with an outside carrier at a rate the carrier already agreed to.
- cancel_carrier_assignment — Take the outside carrier off a move that has not started, leaving it uncovered, and void the carrier's rate confirmation.
- list_shipment_tenders — List a shipment's tenders, newest first, with every offer in rank order.
- record_tender_response — Record a carrier's answer to a tender offer that reached you by phone or email instead of through the offer's link.
- list_rate_confirmations — List a move's rate confirmations, newest revision first.
- generate_rate_confirmation — Generate the rate confirmation for a move covered by an outside carrier.
- send_rate_confirmation — Email a rate confirmation to the carrier, with a link to sign it while it is unsigned.
- void_rate_confirmation — Void a rate confirmation so the revision stops standing and its sign link stops working.
- record_rate_confirmation_confirmed — Record that the carrier confirmed a rate confirmation outside its sign link, for instance by signing and returning the PDF or agreeing on the phone.
- list_edi_partners — List this organization's EDI trading partners with their code, name and the customer each stands for.
- list_edi_transfers — List EDI load tender transfers, the tenders partners sent in or this organization sent out.
- get_edi_transfer — Retrieve one EDI load tender by id, with its stops, freight and rate and the mappings it still lacks.
- send_edi_tender — Propose tendering a New shipment to another organization on Trenova over EDI, which it accepts or declines on its side.
- cancel_edi_tender — Propose withdrawing a load tender this organization sent to another organization over EDI and that it has not yet answered.
- expire_edi_tender — Propose closing an EDI load tender that went unanswered past the time it had to be answered in, sent or received.
- list_edi_transfer_changes — List statuses and cancellations the other organization on an EDI-linked load reported, newest first.
- review_edi_transfer_change — Propose applying or rejecting a status or cancellation the other organization on an EDI-linked load reported.
- list_edi_messages — List EDI documents sent to or received from trading partners, newest first, with delivery status, attempts, the last delivery error and acknowledgment.
- send_edi_status_update — Propose sending a trading partner an EDI 214 shipment status built from a shipment or a service failure.
- retry_edi_message_delivery — Propose sending outbound EDI documents that failed to reach their trading partner again, over the partner's communication profile.
- replay_edi_message — Propose sending an outbound EDI document its trading partner already received once more, exactly as it was generated.
- uncancel_shipment — Reopen a canceled shipment as New, with its moves and stops back to New, when the person says the freight is back on.
- duplicate_shipment — Copy an existing shipment into new ones on the server, carrying its customer, stops, commodities, charges, freight terms and rating method exactly as saved.
- update_shipment_hold — Change an active hold on a shipment: its severity, its notes, what it blocks (dispatch, delivery, billing) and whether the customer sees it.
- split_move_at_relay — Split a two-stop move at its delivery stop so the freight is dropped there as a relay and a new move carries it on to a new delivery location.
- recalculate_shipment_distance — Work out a shipment's move miles again from its stops through the organization's distance profile and routing provider, and save them.
- transfer_shipment_ownership — Make another person the owner of a shipment, the one it is filed under and who is asked about it.
- pin_shipment_comment — Pin a comment to the top of a shipment's thread so dispatch sees it first.
- resolve_shipment_comment — Mark a comment on a shipment resolved once what it asked for is done, or reopen one with resolved=false when it is not.
- generate_recurring_shipment — Create the shipment for a recurring shipment's next slot now, or for the slot at occurrenceAt, instead of waiting for the schedule.
- update_shipment — Change the details of a saved shipment: the customer, service type, shipment type, equipment types, BOL, pieces, weight or temperature range.

How a task is done with these, in order, each step's result feeding the next; skip a step whose answer you already have:
- assign_move: get_shipment → rank_move_candidates → assign_move
- place_shipment_hold: get_shipment → search_shipments → explain_rate → quote_shipment → list_hold_reasons → place_shipment_hold
- assign_move_to_carrier: shop_carriers → assign_move_to_carrier → generate_rate_confirmation
- send_rate_confirmation: list_rate_confirmations → generate_rate_confirmation → send_rate_confirmation
- send_edi_tender: search_shipments → list_edi_partners → send_edi_tender → list_edi_transfers
- cancel_edi_tender: list_edi_transfers → cancel_edi_tender
- expire_edi_tender: list_edi_transfers → expire_edi_tender
- review_edi_transfer_change: get_shipment_tracking → list_edi_transfer_changes → review_edi_transfer_change
- update_shipment: search_shipments → get_shipment → update_shipment
